{"id":"word:hebrew:H1","type":"word","title":"אָב","subtitle":"H1 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"father , in a literal and immediate, or figurative and remote application","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אָב (H1) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 1213 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אָב (ʼâb) means father , in a literal and immediate, or figurative and remote application First listed occurrence: 1Chr 2 17."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אָב","transliteration":"ʼâb","pronunciation":"awb","strong":"H1","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["אָבִ֑י/ו","אָבִֽי/ו","אָבִ֔י/ו","אָבִ֖י/ו","אֲבִ֣י"],"morphs":[["HNcmsc/Sp3ms",199],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",124],["HNcmpc/Sp3mp",112],["HNcmsc/Sp2ms",96],["HNcmpc/Sp3ms",76],["HNcmsc",72],["HNcmpc/Sp2mp",53],["HNcmpc/Sp1cp",38],["HTd/Ncmpa",36],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",35]]},"definitions":{"short":"father , in a literal and immediate, or figurative and remote application","usage":"chief, (fore-) father(-less), × patrimony, principal. Compare names in 'Abi-'.","full":"H1. ab אָב 1191 noun masculine father (Phoenician אב , Assyrian abu , Arabic , Sabean אב CIS iv, 1, 37 1. 2 and others, Ethiopic Aramaic אַבָּא , — absolute אָב Gen 44:19 47t.; construct אַב 17:4-5 , (compare in אַבְרָהָם ib. & elsewhere in proper names. On Hal's proposed אֲבִר see אברהם ); אֲבִי (compare Ge §§ 90, 3 b , 96 ) 4:20 +; suffix אָבִי 19:34 + (MI אבי ); אָבִיךָ 12:1 +; אָבִיו 2:24 +; אָבִ֫יהוּ Judg 14:10 + 6t.; plural אָבוֺת Exod 12:3 +; construct אֲבוֺת 6:25 7 t.; suffix אֲבוֺתַי ( אֲבוֺתָ֑י אֲבֹתַי, ) Gen 47:9 15 t.; אֲבוֺתֵיהֶם 1Chr 4:38 32 t. (late); אֲבוֺתָם Exod 4:5 106t. etc.; — 1 father of individual Gen 2:24 (+ אֵם ) 11:28-29 , (twice in verse); 19:31-32 , 33 , + often (mostly J E D); of father as commanding 50:16 (J) Jer 35:6 f Prov 6:20 (compare Gen 18:19 ; J 28:1 , 6 P 1Sam 17:20 ; 1Kin 2:1 ); instructing מוסר Prov 1:8 ; 4:1 (compare Deut 8:5 ); specifically as begetter, genitor Prov 23:22 ; Zech 13:3 (twice in verse) (+ אֵם ) Isa 45:10 ; compare Gen 49:4 (J) Lev 18:7-8 , 11 (P); rebuking Gen 37:10 ; loving 37:4 ; 44:20 (J E; compare 22:2 ; 25:28 ; 37:3 ; 2Sam 14:1 ); pitying Psa 103:13 (in simile compare 2Sam 18:5 ); blessing Gen 27:41 (J E compare 27:4 ; also 28:1 P +); as glad Prov 10:1 ; 15:20 ; compare 29:3 ; grieving Gen 37:35 (J E; compare 2Sam 12:22 ; 19:1 ; 19:2 f) etc. Also as object of honour, obedience, love Exod 20:12 (E) = Deut 5:16 ; Exod 21:15 , 17 (E) Deut 21:18-19 , Gen 28:7 (P) 1Kin 19:20 (all + אֵם ), 1Ki 50:1; 1Ki 50:5 (J) Mal 1:6 etc. Hence metaphor of intimate connection Job 17:14 to corruption I cry, My father art thou (|| לָֽרִמָּה וַאֲחֹתִי אִמִּי ). 2 of God as father of his people (see RS Sem 42 ), who constituted, controls, guides and lovingly watches over it: Deut 32:6 ; Jer 3:4 , 19 ; 31:9 ; Isa 63:16 (twice in verse); 64:7 ; Mal 1:6 ; 2:10 (compare Exod 4:22 ; 19:4 (JE) Deut 32:11 ; Hosea 11:1 ); compare Jer 2:27 (of idolatrous Israel) ילדתני׃ אַתְּ וְלָאֶבֶן אַתָּה אָבִי לָעֵץ אֹמְרִים ; especially God as father of Davidic line 2Sam 7:14 ; Psa 89:27 ; f. of needy (late) 68:6 (compare 103:13 ) (in proper name, f. of individual , compare below) 3 head of household , family or clan; אָבִי בֵּית as abode Gen 38:11 (twice in verse); Lev 22:13 +; = family Gen 24:40 (|| מִשְׁמַּחְתִּי ) 41:51 ; 46:31 +? Num 18:1-2 , Josh 2:12 , 18 ; 6:25 ; especially techn. of divisions of Israel לְמִשְׁמָּחוֺת אָב בֵּית Num 3:30 , 35 = a father's house, i.e. a family or clan; more often plural ( אבותיו אבותם, ) אָבוֺת בֵית = father's houses = families, clans (compare Di on Exod 6:14 ) 6:14 ; 12:3 ; Num 1:2 , 18 ff (often in Numbers) Josh 14:1 ; 19:51 ; 21:1 (twice in verse); 22:14 (twice in verse) (always P in Hexateuch); also 1Chr 5:13 , 15 + often in Chronicles; compare הלוים אבות רָאשֵׁי (= ׳ר א ׳בית ) Exod 6:25 compare 1Kin 8:1 ; 1Chr 6:4 ; 7:11 +? Ezra Nehemiah. 4 ancestor ( a ) of individual; grandfather (instead of precise term) Gen 28:13 ; 32:10 (J; where used by Jacob of Abraham & then of Isaac); greatgrandfather 1Kin 15:13 ; great-greatgrandfather 15:11 etc.; oft plural (= fathers, forefathers ) Gen 15:15 ; 46:34 (JE) 1Kin 19:4 ; 21:3-4 , 2Kin 19:12 ; 20:17 +; particularly אבותיו עם שׁכב 1Kin 1:21 ; 2:10 ; 11:21 ; 22:40 +; joined with אב עם ׳ויקבר 14:31 ; 15:24 ; 22:51 ; 2Kin 8:24 ; 15:38 compare 15:7 , 16:20 + (all of kings of Judah); intensive, אֲבֹתֶיךָ וַאֲבוֺת אֲבֹתֶיךָ Exod 10:6 compare Dan 11:24 ; ( b ) of people Gen 10:21 (J) 17:4-5 , (P) 19:37-38 , (J) 36:9 , 43 (P) Deut 26:5 ; Isa 51:2 ; 43:27 (where הראשׁון אביך thy first father , see Che) compare also Ezek 16:3 , 45 + often; plural Exod 3:13 , 15 , 16 (E) Deut 1:8 ; Josh 1:6 ; Judg 2:1 ; 1Sam 12:6 +; 12:15 near the end read ᵐ5 וּבְמַלְכְּכֶם We Dr. 5 originator or patron of a class, profession, or art Gen 4:20-21 ,. 6 figurative of producer, Generator Job 38:28 אָ֑ב לַמָּטָר הֲיֵשׁ (|| מִיֿ אֶגְלֵיטָֽֿל׃ הוֺלִיד ). 7 figurative of benevolence & protection Job 29:6 לָֽאֶבְיוֺנִים אָֽנֹכִי אָב , compare 31:18 ; of Eliakim Isa 22:21 ; perhaps also of gracious Messianic king עַד אֲבִי 9:5 everlasting father (Ge Ew De Che Brd Di) — others divider of spoil (Abarb Hi Kn Kue Br MP ). 8 term of respect & honour ( Abbas, Pater, Papa, Pope ); applied to master 2Kin 5:13 ; priest Judg 17:10 ; 18:19 ; prophet 2Kin 2:12 (twice in verse); 6:21 ; 13:14 (twice in verse); compare 8:9 ; counsellor Gen 45:8 (E; compare δευτέρου πατρός ᵐ5 add. Est 3:13 ; τῷ πατρί 1Mac Esth 11:32); king 1Sam 24:12 ; artificer 2Chr 2:12 ; 4:16 . 9 specifically, ruler, chief (late) 1Chr 2:24 , 42 (twice in verse); etc. (compare Ew § 273 b ) see also Ew Geschichte. i. 524. H i. 365 . On the force of אָב in proper names (in many probably a divine title), see Che Ency. Bib., ABI, NAMES WITH Nö ib., NAMES, §§ 44, 45 . א , Aleph , first letter; in post Biblical Hebrew = numeral 1 (and so in margin of printed MT); א֟ = 1000; no evidence of this usage in OT times. אָב see II. אבה . אבב ( fresh, bright , Assyrian abâbu Dl w , AGI.)","rootNote":"a primitive word;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 2 17","keyReferences":["1Chr 2 17","1Chr 2 21","1Chr 2 23","1Chr 2 24","1Chr 2 42","1Chr 2 42","1Chr 2 44","1Chr 2 45"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":1213,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 2 17","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/אֲבִ֣י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 21","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":21,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲבִ֣י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 23","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲבִי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 24","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲבִ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 42","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":42,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲבִי","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 42","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":42,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲבִ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 44","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":44,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲבִ֣י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 45","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":45,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲבִ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 49","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":49,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲבִ֣י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 49","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":49,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֲבִ֥י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcmsc"},{"reference":"1Chr 2 49","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":49,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/אֲבִ֣י","so